      <article class="article">

        <h2>Why Kiwis Love the Gold Coast</h2>
        <p>The Gold Coast is the most popular beach destination for Kiwis moving to Australia. With 57 kilometres of coastline, 300 sunny days a year, and a massive Kiwi community, it feels like the ultimate upgrade. The cost of living is lower than Sydney and Melbourne, and Brisbane's job market is just an hour's train ride north.</p>
        <p>The Gold Coast has grown from a holiday town into a genuine city — with its own university (Griffith), hospital network, light rail system, and growing tech scene. The 2018 Commonwealth Games transformed the infrastructure, and the 2032 Olympics (with events on the GC) will bring another wave of development.</p>

        <h2>Jobs on the Gold Coast</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Tourism &amp; hospitality</strong> — The backbone of the GC economy. Hotels, theme parks, restaurants, and events. Year-round hiring.</li>
          <li><strong>Construction &amp; trades</strong> — High-rise development in Surfers Paradise, Broadbeach, and Southport is constant. Trades workers in high demand.</li>
          <li><strong>Healthcare</strong> — Gold Coast University Hospital is one of Australia's newest. Nursing and allied health roles available.</li>
          <li><strong>Education</strong> — Griffith University, Bond University, and TAFE. Teaching and support roles.</li>
          <li><strong>Marine &amp; water sports</strong> — Surf schools, boat building, marine services. Niche but growing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Salaries on the Gold Coast are typically 10–15% lower than Brisbane for the same role. Many GC residents commute to Brisbane for higher-paying jobs — the train takes about 70 minutes from Helensvale to Brisbane Central.</p>

        <h2>Cost of Living on the Gold Coast</h2>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Monthly Expense</th>
                <th>Beachside (AUD)</th>
                <th>Hinterland/Outer (AUD)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>2-bed apartment rent</td><td class="price">$2,000–$2,800</td><td class="price">$1,500–$2,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Groceries (couple)</td><td>$450–$600</td><td>$420–$560</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Public transport (go card)</td><td>$100–$140</td><td>$120–$160</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Utilities</td><td>$180–$260</td><td>$170–$240</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Car (almost essential)</td><td>$300–$500</td><td>$300–$500</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>A car is more important on the Gold Coast than in Sydney or Melbourne. The light rail covers the coastal strip, but suburbs inland are car-dependent.</p>

        <h2>Best Suburbs for Kiwis on the Gold Coast</h2>

        <div class="checklist-box">
          <h3>Kiwi communities &amp; affordable</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Coomera / Pimpama / Ormeau</strong> — Northern Gold Coast. Newest housing estates, very affordable. Huge Kiwi and Pacific Islander community. Train to Brisbane. Near Dreamworld and Movie World.</li>
            <li><strong>Nerang</strong> — Inland, affordable, central to everything. Good base for families.</li>
            <li><strong>Southport</strong> — Central Gold Coast hub. Light rail access, Chinatown precinct, close to the Broadwater. Mix of apartments and houses.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-box" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3>Beach lifestyle</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Burleigh Heads</strong> — Best surf, best vibe. James Street cafés, national park. Very popular with Kiwi surfers. Pricier but worth it.</li>
            <li><strong>Palm Beach / Currumbin</strong> — Southern GC. Quieter, family-friendly beaches. Strong community feel.</li>
            <li><strong>Broadbeach</strong> — Restaurants, casino, light rail. More upmarket than Surfers. Popular with working professionals.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-box" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3>Hinterland</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Mudgeeraba / Robina</strong> — Inland, leafy, family-oriented. Robina Town Centre is a major shopping hub. Good schools.</li>
            <li><strong>Tamborine Mountain</strong> — Rainforest living, cooler temperatures, stunning views. 30 min to the beach. Popular with Kiwis escaping the heat.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Shipping from NZ to the Gold Coast</h2>
        <p>Gold Coast shipments arrive via the Port of Brisbane (about 70km north). Your mover handles the trucking from port to your GC address.</p>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Move Size</th>
                <th>Estimated Cost (NZD)</th>
                <th>Transit Time</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Boxes only (1–10)</td><td class="price">$900–$2,200</td><td>3–4 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>1-bed apartment</td><td class="price">$2,500–$5,000</td><td>3–5 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>2–3 bed house</td><td class="price">$5,000–$9,000</td><td>3–5 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>4+ bed house</td><td class="price">$9,000–$14,500</td><td>4–5 weeks</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Read our <a href="/shipping-to-australia-from-nz">complete NZ to Australia shipping guide</a> for customs, biosecurity, and tips.</p>

        <h2>Getting Around the Gold Coast</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Light rail (G:link)</strong> — runs from Helensvale to Broadbeach South along the coast. Fast and reliable.</li>
          <li><strong>Trains</strong> — heavy rail connects Varsity Lakes to Brisbane via Helensvale and Coomera.</li>
          <li><strong>Car</strong> — essential for most suburbs. Parking is usually free outside the tourist strip.</li>
          <li><strong>NZ licence</strong> — valid for 3 months, then swap to QLD licence (no test for Kiwis).</li>
        </ul>

